{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>And you shall set the table.</b> The table in the north, drawn from the northern wall two cubits and a half; and the menorah in the south, drawn from the southern wall two cubits and a half; and the golden altar set opposite the open space between the table and the menorah, drawn slightly toward the east. And all of them are placed from the middle of the Mishkan inward. How so? The length of the Mishkan from the entrance to the veil is twenty cubits; the altar and the table and the menorah are drawn from the entrance toward the west ten cubits (Yoma 33)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:51.633023638Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}